SECTION 23 — PROGRESS CALCULATION RULES

This section is extremely important.

Every displayed metric must have a defined calculation.

Examples:

Habit completion percentage:

Completed scheduled occurrences / Total eligible scheduled occurrences × 100.

Task completion percentage:

Completed tasks / Total tasks in the selected reporting period × 100.

Goal progress:

Actual recorded value / Target value × 100, capped or displayed appropriately according to the target type.

Study target completion:

Actual study hours / Target study hours × 100.

Workout consistency:

Completed scheduled workout sessions / Scheduled workout sessions × 100.

Overall progress:

Use configurable, normalized category scores with clearly disclosed weights.

Do not mix raw hours, task counts and percentages without normalization.

Do not count unscheduled days as failures.

Do not treat an archived habit as a current missed habit.

Do not double-count a calendar event and its original activity record.

Allow the user to inspect how a score was calculated.

